cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research package, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Fiscal Choke Points: Transaction-Node Architecture and Operational Fiscal Capacity in Southeast Asian Digital Tax Administration"
authors:
  - family-names: Ongko
    given-names: Christopher
    affiliation: "Yuan Ze University"
version: "DT-FCP-2026-001"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Spectating101/solarpunk-coin"
url: "https://github.com/Spectating101/solarpunk-coin/tree/digital-tax/rebuild-2026/IE-JDE/Digital_Tax_Design/rebuilt_2026"
abstract: >-
  A source-controlled comparative research package examining how five Southeast
  Asian jurisdictions assign bounded fiscal functions to nodes inside seven
  digital-tax transaction paths. The package separates taxable object, liable
  node, destination or nexus evidence, transaction rail, and reconciliation
  power; distinguishes node locus from event coupling; and preserves explicit
  boundaries between legal architecture and operational performance. The work
  is comparative and institutional rather than causal.
keywords:
  - digital taxation
  - tax administration
  - VAT
  - GST
  - e-commerce
  - regulatory intermediaries
  - transaction paths
  - Southeast Asia
